**Total Must-have points:** 55 | **Should:** 11 | **Could:** 8

## MVP definition

The **Minimum Viable Product** is the smallest release that lets a customer open an account end to end without visiting a branch:

US-01 to US-08 (all Must-haves). Without any one of these, the journey does not work.

## Suggested release plan (2-week sprints, assuming a velocity of about 14 points per sprint for a new team)

| Sprint | Goal | Stories |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Customer can register and enter details | US-01, US-02 |
| 2 | Customer can capture ID; verification integration starts | US-03, start US-04 |
| 3 | Verification and referral queue work | finish US-04, US-05 |
| 4 | Account creation and signing work | US-06, US-07 |
| 5 | Confirmation, virtual card, hardening and pilot readiness | US-08, US-09 |
| 6 | Reporting and branch assistance | US-10, US-11 |

**MVP pilot** after Sprint 5 with a limited group of customers (for example, staff and a single branch region) before full launch.

## Success measures for the pilot

| Measure | Target |
|---|---|
| Straight-through processing rate | 85% or higher |
| Median time to open an account | under 15 minutes |
| Abandonment rate | under 15% |
| Referral resolution time | under 4 working hours |
| Customer satisfaction (post-onboarding survey) | 4 out of 5 or higher |
